  m_Text: "This scene demonstrates how to dynamically mount or parent an object to
    an UMA bone while at runtime.\n\nIn addition to using these methods, you can
    also simply tag the object, and parent it to a bone, as long as you put the \"UMAIgnore\"
    tag on the item. \n\n2.10 - Examine the \"UMAMountObject\" component on the UMADynamicCharacterAvatar
    for an example of how to mount objects to an UMA Skeleton.\n\n2.11 - You can
    also use UMAMountedItem to mount objects to a character. Using this method has
    slightly more overhead, but the item survives a rebuild, and does not need to
    be re-attached.\n"
